-- Adapted practice based on the supplied Access 2 G9 Unit 1 pages.
-- Adds shared learning content under the existing approved-reader/tutor RLS policies.
insert into public.lessons (id, week, title, description, objectives, activities, activities_kk, homework, duration, skill, book_unit, book_page, practice_path)
select id, week, title, description, objectives, activities, activities_kk, homework, duration, skill, book_unit, book_page, practice_path from jsonb_populate_recordset(null::public.lessons, $access2$
[{"id":"access2-u1-1","week":1,"title":"Holidays and the weather","description":"Use was/were to describe a holiday. Match travel phrases and weather words.","objectives":["Use was/were to describe a holiday. Match travel phrases and weather words."],"activities":"Use was with I/he/she/it and were with you/we/they. Negatives: wasn't/weren't. Put was/were before the subject in a question. Say go by bus, go on holiday, and go swimming. Organise a holiday paragraph with an introduction, details, and an ending.","activities_kk":"I/he/she/it есімдіктерімен was, you/we/they есімдіктерімен were қолданылады. Болымсыз түрлері: wasn't/weren't. Сұрақта was/were бастауыштың алдына қойылады. Тіркестер: go by bus, go on holiday, go swimming. Мәтінде кіріспе, негізгі бөлім және қорытынды болсын.","homework":"Write 6–8 sentences about a real or imaginary holiday. Include where you were, who was with you, two weather words, two activities, and one negative sentence. Add a title and a short caption for a drawing. Use pages 10–13.","duration":25,"skill":"Grammar","book_unit":"Access 2 · Unit 1","book_page":"10–13","practice_path":"/practice?lesson=access2-u1-1"},{"id":"access2-u1-2","week":2,"title":"A new neighbour: past verbs","description":"Practise regular and irregular past forms, then retell a short visit.","objectives":["Practise regular and irregular past forms, then retell a short visit."],"activities":"Regular verbs usually take -ed: call → called, move → moved. Learn irregular forms: go → went, see → saw, write → wrote, take → took. Read the dialogue on page 14 and notice why Lucy is upset. For -ed pronunciation, compare walked /t/, played /d/, and wanted /ɪd/.","activities_kk":"Дұрыс етістіктерге әдетте -ed жалғанады: call → called, move → moved. Бұрыс түрлерді жатта: go → went, see → saw, write → wrote, take → took. 14-беттегі диалогты оқып, Lucy неге ренжігенін түсіндір. -ed дыбысталуы: walked /t/, played /d/, wanted /ɪd/.","homework":"Read page 14. Explain in two English sentences why Lucy is upset and what she does next. Then write six sentences about a visit last weekend using three regular and three irregular past verbs. Use pages 15–16 to check the forms.","duration":25,"skill":"Grammar","book_unit":"Access 2 · Unit 1","book_page":"14–16","practice_path":"/practice?lesson=access2-u1-2"},{"id":"access2-u1-3","week":3,"title":"Understanding words in context","description":"Use context clues and retell the pony story in the right order.","objectives":["Use context clues and retell the pony story in the right order."],"activities":"Read the whole sentence before looking up a new word. A nearby explanation, a picture, or a familiar word part can help. On page 17, cottage is explained as a little house. Write the clue as well as your guess. Retell only the main events, in order.","activities_kk":"Жаңа сөзді іздемес бұрын сөйлемді толық оқы. Жанындағы түсіндірме, сурет не таныс сөз бөлігі көмектеседі. 17-бетте cottage шағын үй ретінде сипатталған. Болжамыңмен бірге оған негіз болған белгіні жаз. Негізгі оқиғаларды ретімен баянда.","homework":"Read A pony came to tea on page 17. Choose five unfamiliar words, guess their meanings, and explain the clue for each. Then retell the story in 4–5 English sentences: arrival, the open house, the pony, the damage, and the ending. Use your own words.","duration":25,"skill":"Reading","book_unit":"Access 2 · Unit 1","book_page":"17","practice_path":"/reading/access2-pony"},{"id":"access2-u1-4","week":4,"title":"Questions and phone conversations","description":"Ask past questions with did and practise a polite phone call.","objectives":["Ask past questions with did and practise a polite phone call."],"activities":"Use Did + subject + base verb: Did you see Leo? Say Yes, I did or No, I didn't. For information, add Where, When, What, Why, or How before did. In a phone call, introduce yourself, ask for the person, and offer to leave a message.","activities_kk":"Құрылым: Did + бастауыш + етістіктің бастапқы түрі: Did you see Leo? Қысқа жауап: Yes, I did немесе No, I didn't. Ақпарат сұрау үшін did алдына Where, When, What, Why не How қой. Телефонда өзіңді таныстыр, керек адамды сұра, хабарлама қалдыруды ұсын.","homework":"Write five questions about a friend's holiday: one yes/no question and four wh-questions. Answer them in English. Then write a six-line phone dialogue in which the person you want is not at home and you leave a message. Refer to pages 18–21. Audio tasks need the book's recordings.","duration":25,"skill":"Grammar","book_unit":"Access 2 · Unit 1","book_page":"18–21","practice_path":"/practice?lesson=access2-u1-4"},{"id":"access2-u1-5","week":5,"title":"Abby's news: negatives and feelings","description":"Understand the characters' feelings and use didn't + base verb.","objectives":["Understand the characters' feelings and use didn't + base verb."],"activities":"After didn't, use the base verb: She didn't go, not She didn't went. In Abby's news, distinguish what happened from how each person feels. Support feelings with a detail from the text. Don't confuse bored (a person's feeling) with boring (a description).","activities_kk":"Didn't сөзінен кейін етістіктің бастапқы түрі келеді: She didn't go. She didn't went деу қате. Abby's news мәтінінде оқиғаны кейіпкердің сезімінен ажырат. Сезімді мәтіндегі дерекпен дәлелде. Bored — адамның сезімі, boring — бір нәрсенің сипаты.","homework":"Read Abby's news on page 22 and use page 23 to check your understanding. Write one sentence about Abby's news, two about Maya's feelings with evidence, and four sentences about your own weekend: two positive and two negative. Use didn't with the base verb.","duration":25,"skill":"Grammar","book_unit":"Access 2 · Unit 1","book_page":"22–25","practice_path":"/practice?lesson=access2-u1-5"},{"id":"access2-u1-6","week":6,"title":"Notes and everyday English","description":"Prepare a crib sheet and turn it into a short spoken story.","objectives":["Prepare a crib sheet and turn it into a short spoken story."],"activities":"Before speaking, note keywords for where, when, who, weather, activities, and feelings. Use arrows or symbols that you understand. Speak from the notes rather than reading a full script. Page 27 also practises polite phone phrases; its video tasks require the original video.","activities_kk":"Сөйлеу алдында қайда, қашан, кіммен, ауа райы, әрекеттер және сезімдер туралы тірек сөздерді жаз. Өзің түсінетін белгілер мен бағыттауыштарды қолдан. Толық мәтінді оқымай, тірек жазбаға сүйеніп сөйле. 27-бетте телефон тіркестері бар; бейне тапсырмасына бастапқы бейне қажет.","homework":"Using page 26, make a crib sheet for one holiday day: place, people, weather, three activities, and a feeling. Practise a one-minute talk with it. Submit your notes and a 4–6 sentence English retelling. Add a four-line lost-phone dialogue using page 27. Your tutor will assess speaking in the lesson.","duration":25,"skill":"Speaking","book_unit":"Access 2 · Unit 1","book_page":"26–27","practice_path":"/writing?assignment=access2-u1-6"},{"id":"access2-u1-7","week":7,"title":"My USA logbook","description":"Follow a travel diary and describe events with irregular past verbs.","objectives":["Follow a travel diary and describe events with irregular past verbs."],"activities":"Read the dated entries on pages 28–29. Match each event to its place, and use the dates to order events. Notice buy → bought, eat → ate, hear → heard, and wake up → woke up. A diary can describe past events and then say how the writer feels now.","activities_kk":"28–29-беттердегі күнделік жазбаларын оқы. Әр оқиғаны орнымен сәйкестендіріп, күндер бойынша ретте. Түрлерге назар аудар: buy → bought, eat → ate, hear → heard, wake up → woke up. Күнделікте өткен оқиғаны, содан кейін қазіргі сезімді жазуға болады.","homework":"Read My USA logbook on pages 28–29. List four activities Justin did and where he did them. Write two short diary entries about a real or imagined trip, using at least five past-tense verbs. Include one surprising event and how you felt. Review the irregular verbs on page 207.","duration":25,"skill":"Reading","book_unit":"Access 2 · Unit 1","book_page":"28–29, 206–207","practice_path":"/reading/access2-logbook"},{"id":"access2-u1-8","week":8,"title":"A holiday brochure and reflection","description":"Create a clear holiday page and reflect on what you can do.","objectives":["Create a clear holiday page and reflect on what you can do."],"activities":"Plan a brochure page with a heading, introduction, activities, weather, and a recommendation. Use the present for general facts and the past for what you did. Include captions and credit any pictures you use. Check vocabulary, notes, grammar, and layout before sharing.","activities_kk":"Буклет бетіне тақырып, кіріспе, әрекеттер, ауа райы және ұсыныс жоспарла. Жалпы мәліметке осы шақты, өзің жасаған әрекетке өткен шақты қолдан. Суретке жазу қосып, дереккөзін көрсет. Бөлісер алдында сөздерді, жазбаларды, грамматиканы және орналасуын тексер.","homework":"Using pages 30–31, write a 80–100 word brochure page about a place in Germany, Kazakhstan, or another country. Include the season, location, weather, three things visitors can do, and what you did or would like to do. Add a heading and caption. Finish by rating your vocabulary, notes, grammar, and layout: needs practice, OK, or confident.","duration":25,"skill":"Writing","book_unit":"Access 2 · Unit 1","book_page":"30–31","practice_path":"/writing?assignment=access2-u1-8"}]
$access2$::jsonb) on conflict (id) do nothing;

insert into public.quiz_questions (id, lesson_id, topic, difficulty, type, prompt, options, answer, explanation, explanation_kk)
select id, lesson_id, topic, difficulty, type, prompt, options, answer, explanation, explanation_kk from jsonb_populate_recordset(null::public.quiz_questions, $access2$
[{"id":"access2-q01","lesson_id":"access2-u1-1","topic":"Past simple: be","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"choice","prompt":"I ___ at the seaside last August.","options":["was","were","am"],"answer":"was","explanation":"Use was with I for a finished time in the past.","explanation_kk":"Өткен уақыт туралы I есімдігімен was қолданылады."},{"id":"access2-q02","lesson_id":"access2-u1-1","topic":"Past simple: be","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"choice","prompt":"We ___ in New York. We were in Boston.","options":["wasn't","weren't","isn't"],"answer":"weren't","explanation":"Use weren't with we for a negative past statement.","explanation_kk":"We есімдігімен өткен шақта болымсыз weren't қолданылады."},{"id":"access2-q03","lesson_id":"access2-u1-1","topic":"Past simple: be","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"choice","prompt":"___ the weather warm yesterday?","options":["Was","Were","Did"],"answer":"Was","explanation":"Put was before the subject to ask about a past state.","explanation_kk":"Өткен жағдайды сұрағанда was бастауыштың алдына қойылады."},{"id":"access2-q04","lesson_id":"access2-u1-1","topic":"Holiday vocabulary","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"choice","prompt":"We travelled ___ train.","options":["by","on","at"],"answer":"by","explanation":"Say go or travel by train, bus, or car.","explanation_kk":"Көлікпен баруды by train, by bus, by car деп айтамыз."},{"id":"access2-q05","lesson_id":"access2-u1-1","topic":"Holiday vocabulary","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"choice","prompt":"They went ___ holiday in July.","options":["by","on","in"],"answer":"on","explanation":"The phrase is go on holiday.","explanation_kk":"Дұрыс тіркес — go on holiday."},{"id":"access2-q06","lesson_id":"access2-u1-1","topic":"Holiday vocabulary","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"choice","prompt":"There were lots of clouds. It was ___.","options":["cloudy","sunny","hot"],"answer":"cloudy","explanation":"Cloudy describes a sky with many clouds.","explanation_kk":"Cloudy — аспанды бұлт басқан деген сөз."},{"id":"access2-q07","lesson_id":"access2-u1-2","topic":"Past simple","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"choice","prompt":"Yesterday Lucy ___ her mum.","options":["called","calls","calling"],"answer":"called","explanation":"Call is regular: add -ed to make called.","explanation_kk":"Call — дұрыс етістік. Өткен шақта -ed жалғанады."},{"id":"access2-q08","lesson_id":"access2-u1-2","topic":"Past simple","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"choice","prompt":"Last Saturday Tom ___ to Plymouth.","options":["go","went","goed"],"answer":"went","explanation":"Go has the irregular past form went.","explanation_kk":"Go етістігінің бұрыс өткен шақ түрі — went."},{"id":"access2-q09","lesson_id":"access2-u1-2","topic":"Past simple","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"blank","prompt":"Sam ___ (see) a new neighbour yesterday.","options":[],"answer":"saw","explanation":"The past form of see is saw.","explanation_kk":"See етістігінің өткен шақ түрі — saw."},{"id":"access2-q10","lesson_id":"access2-u1-2","topic":"Past simple","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"blank","prompt":"Lucy ___ (write) a message after the call.","options":[],"answer":"wrote","explanation":"The past form of write is wrote.","explanation_kk":"Write етістігінің өткен шақ түрі — wrote."},{"id":"access2-q11","lesson_id":"access2-u1-2","topic":"Past simple","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"choice","prompt":"Which verb ends with the sound /ɪd/?","options":["wanted","played","walked"],"answer":"wanted","explanation":"Wanted has an extra /ɪd/ syllable after the /t/ sound.","explanation_kk":"Wanted сөзінде /t/ дыбысынан кейін /ɪd/ буыны айтылады."},{"id":"access2-q12","lesson_id":"access2-u1-4","topic":"Past simple: questions","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"choice","prompt":"Did you ___ table tennis yesterday?","options":["play","played","plays"],"answer":"play","explanation":"After did, use the base form of the verb.","explanation_kk":"Did сөзінен кейін етістіктің бастапқы түрі қолданылады."},{"id":"access2-q13","lesson_id":"access2-u1-4","topic":"Past simple: questions","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"choice","prompt":"___ did you go? — By bus.","options":["How","Where","When"],"answer":"How","explanation":"How asks about the way you travelled.","explanation_kk":"How — қалай барғаныңды сұрайды."},{"id":"access2-q14","lesson_id":"access2-u1-4","topic":"Past simple: questions","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"choice","prompt":"___ did you visit your cousins? — Last week.","options":["Why","When","Who"],"answer":"When","explanation":"When asks about time.","explanation_kk":"When уақытты сұрайды."},{"id":"access2-q15","lesson_id":"access2-u1-4","topic":"Past simple: questions","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"choice","prompt":"Did Maya visit the farm? — Yes, she ___.","options":["did","does","was"],"answer":"did","explanation":"Use did in a short answer to a did question.","explanation_kk":"Did бар сұрақтың қысқа жауабында did қолданылады."},{"id":"access2-q16","lesson_id":"access2-u1-4","topic":"Phone conversations","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"choice","prompt":"You want to speak to Sam. Choose the polite request.","options":["Can I speak to Sam, please?","Sam speaks yesterday.","I speaking Sam."],"answer":"Can I speak to Sam, please?","explanation":"Can I speak to ... please? is a polite phone request.","explanation_kk":"Can I speak to ... please? — телефондағы сыпайы өтініш."},{"id":"access2-q17","lesson_id":"access2-u1-4","topic":"Phone conversations","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"choice","prompt":"Sam is out. You want him to call later. What can you say?","options":["Can he phone me back, please?","Where did he went?","I am a phone."],"answer":"Can he phone me back, please?","explanation":"Phone me back means call me again later.","explanation_kk":"Phone me back — кейін маған қайта қоңырау шал деген мағына."},{"id":"access2-q18","lesson_id":"access2-u1-5","topic":"Past simple: negatives","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"choice","prompt":"Maya didn't ___ her bike.","options":["ride","rode","rides"],"answer":"ride","explanation":"Didn't already marks the past. Keep ride in its base form.","explanation_kk":"Didn't өткен шақты білдіреді. Ride бастапқы түрде қалады."},{"id":"access2-q19","lesson_id":"access2-u1-5","topic":"Past simple: negatives","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"choice","prompt":"Choose the correct negative sentence.","options":["She didn't go sailing.","She didn't went sailing.","She not went sailing."],"answer":"She didn't go sailing.","explanation":"Use didn't + base verb, even for irregular verbs.","explanation_kk":"Бұрыс етістіктермен де didn't + бастапқы түр қолданылады."},{"id":"access2-q20","lesson_id":"access2-u1-5","topic":"Past simple: negatives","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"correction","prompt":"Correct the sentence: I didn't saw Leo.","options":[],"answer":"I didn't see Leo.","explanation":"After didn't, saw changes back to see.","explanation_kk":"Didn't сөзінен кейін saw емес, see қолданылады."},{"id":"access2-q21","lesson_id":"access2-u1-5","topic":"Past simple: negatives","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"blank","prompt":"They ___ (not play) football yesterday.","options":[],"answer":"didn't play","explanation":"Use didn't + play for a negative past action.","explanation_kk":"Өткен шақтағы болымсыз әрекет үшін didn't + play қолданылады."},{"id":"access2-q22","lesson_id":"access2-u1-5","topic":"Emotions","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"choice","prompt":"Maya had nothing interesting to do. She felt ___.","options":["bored","boring","bore"],"answer":"bored","explanation":"Bored describes a person's feeling; boring describes a thing.","explanation_kk":"Bored — адамның сезімі, boring — бір нәрсенің сипаты."},{"id":"access2-q23","lesson_id":"access2-u1-6","topic":"Study skills","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"choice","prompt":"Which is most useful on a crib sheet?","options":["Short keywords and clear symbols","Every sentence of the whole story","Words you do not understand"],"answer":"Short keywords and clear symbols","explanation":"Notes should help you remember ideas while you speak.","explanation_kk":"Тірек жазба сөйлегенде ойларды еске түсіруге көмектесуі керек."},{"id":"access2-q24","lesson_id":"access2-u1-6","topic":"Phone conversations","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"choice","prompt":"You need the caller to wait. What do you say?","options":["Hold on a minute, please.","You went yesterday.","I am a minute."],"answer":"Hold on a minute, please.","explanation":"Hold on asks someone to wait on the phone.","explanation_kk":"Hold on телефондағы адамнан күте тұруды сұрайды."},{"id":"access2-q25","lesson_id":"access2-u1-7","topic":"Past simple","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"blank","prompt":"On the trip, we ___ (buy) a postcard.","options":[],"answer":"bought","explanation":"The past form of buy is bought.","explanation_kk":"Buy етістігінің өткен шақ түрі — bought."},{"id":"access2-q26","lesson_id":"access2-u1-7","topic":"Past simple","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"blank","prompt":"Dad ___ (eat) two pancakes.","options":[],"answer":"ate","explanation":"The past form of eat is ate.","explanation_kk":"Eat етістігінің өткен шақ түрі — ate."},{"id":"access2-q27","lesson_id":"access2-u1-7","topic":"Past simple","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"blank","prompt":"In the night, Justin ___ (hear) a noise.","options":[],"answer":"heard","explanation":"The past form of hear is heard.","explanation_kk":"Hear етістігінің өткен шақ түрі — heard."},{"id":"access2-q28","lesson_id":"access2-u1-7","topic":"Past simple","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"blank","prompt":"Yesterday I ___ (wake up) early.","options":[],"answer":"woke up","explanation":"The past form of wake up is woke up.","explanation_kk":"Wake up тіркесінің өткен шақ түрі — woke up."},{"id":"access2-q29","lesson_id":"access2-u1-8","topic":"Study skills","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"choice","prompt":"Which order makes a clear holiday paragraph?","options":["Introduction, details, ending","Ending, title, introduction","Random sentences"],"answer":"Introduction, details, ending","explanation":"Introduce the place, add useful details, then finish your idea.","explanation_kk":"Орынды таныстыр, пайдалы мәліметтер қос, кейін ойыңды қорытындыла."},{"id":"access2-q30","lesson_id":"access2-u1-8","topic":"Past simple","difficulty":"Beginner","type":"choice","prompt":"Which sentence describes a finished visit?","options":["We visited the castle last summer.","We visit the castle every summer.","We are visiting the castle now."],"answer":"We visited the castle last summer.","explanation":"Last summer is a finished time, so use the past simple.","explanation_kk":"Last summer — аяқталған уақыт, сондықтан жай өткен шақ қолданылады."}]
$access2$::jsonb) on conflict (id) do nothing;

insert into public.vocabulary (id, word, translation, translation_ru, translation_kk, definition, example, theme, difficulty)
select id, word, translation, translation_ru, translation_kk, definition, example, theme, difficulty from jsonb_populate_recordset(null::public.vocabulary, $access2$
[{"id":"access2-word-1","word":"sunny","translation":"sonnig","translation_ru":"солнечный","translation_kk":"күн ашық","definition":"With bright sunshine.","example":"It was sunny on the beach.","theme":"Weather","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-2","word":"cloudy","translation":"bewölkt","translation_ru":"облачный","translation_kk":"бұлтты","definition":"With many clouds in the sky.","example":"The sky was cloudy yesterday.","theme":"Weather","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-3","word":"rainy","translation":"regnerisch","translation_ru":"дождливый","translation_kk":"жаңбырлы","definition":"With a lot of rain.","example":"We stayed inside on a rainy day.","theme":"Weather","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-4","word":"windy","translation":"windig","translation_ru":"ветреный","translation_kk":"желді","definition":"With a lot of moving air.","example":"It was too windy to play outside.","theme":"Weather","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-5","word":"warm","translation":"warm","translation_ru":"тёплый","translation_kk":"жылы","definition":"A little hot in a comfortable way.","example":"The water was warm.","theme":"Weather","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-6","word":"cold","translation":"kalt","translation_ru":"холодный","translation_kk":"суық","definition":"Having a low temperature.","example":"The sea was cold in April.","theme":"Weather","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-7","word":"hot","translation":"heiß","translation_ru":"жаркий","translation_kk":"ыстық","definition":"Having a high temperature.","example":"It was hot in the afternoon.","theme":"Weather","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-8","word":"go camping","translation":"zelten gehen","translation_ru":"идти в поход с палаткой","translation_kk":"шатырмен демалуға бару","definition":"To stay outdoors in a tent.","example":"We went camping near a lake.","theme":"Holidays","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-9","word":"go sailing","translation":"segeln gehen","translation_ru":"кататься под парусом","translation_kk":"желкенді қайықпен жүзу","definition":"To travel on water in a sailing boat.","example":"They went sailing along the coast.","theme":"Holidays","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-10","word":"postcard","translation":"die Postkarte","translation_ru":"открытка","translation_kk":"ашықхат","definition":"A card with a picture that you can send by post.","example":"I sent a postcard to my grandma.","theme":"Holidays","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-11","word":"campsite","translation":"der Campingplatz","translation_ru":"кемпинг","translation_kk":"шатыр тігетін орын","definition":"A place where people can put up tents.","example":"Our campsite was near a river.","theme":"Holidays","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-12","word":"crib sheet","translation":"der Spickzettel","translation_ru":"листок с заметками","translation_kk":"тірек жазба","definition":"Short notes that help you remember what to say.","example":"My crib sheet had five keywords.","theme":"School","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-13","word":"make notes","translation":"Notizen machen","translation_ru":"делать заметки","translation_kk":"қысқаша жазып алу","definition":"To write down important ideas briefly.","example":"Make notes before your talk.","theme":"School","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-14","word":"boarding school","translation":"das Internat","translation_ru":"школа-интернат","translation_kk":"мектеп-интернат","definition":"A school where students also live.","example":"Her cousin goes to a boarding school.","theme":"School","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-15","word":"term","translation":"das Trimester","translation_ru":"учебный период","translation_kk":"оқу кезеңі","definition":"One part of a school year.","example":"Our new term starts soon.","theme":"School","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-16","word":"rule","translation":"die Regel","translation_ru":"правило","translation_kk":"ереже","definition":"An instruction about what is allowed.","example":"Our class has a rule about phones.","theme":"School","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-17","word":"host family","translation":"die Gastfamilie","translation_ru":"принимающая семья","translation_kk":"қабылдаушы отбасы","definition":"A family you stay with during a visit abroad.","example":"My host family showed me the town.","theme":"School","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-18","word":"get in touch","translation":"Kontakt aufnehmen","translation_ru":"связаться","translation_kk":"хабарласу","definition":"To start communicating with someone.","example":"Please get in touch when you arrive.","theme":"Communication","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-19","word":"stay in touch","translation":"in Kontakt bleiben","translation_ru":"поддерживать связь","translation_kk":"байланысты үзбеу","definition":"To continue communicating with someone.","example":"We stayed in touch after the holiday.","theme":"Communication","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-20","word":"Hold on a minute.","translation":"Bleib einen Moment dran.","translation_ru":"Подожди минуту.","translation_kk":"Бір минут күте тұр.","definition":"A phrase asking someone to wait briefly.","example":"Hold on a minute. I will get Sam.","theme":"Communication","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-21","word":"look forward to","translation":"sich freuen auf","translation_ru":"ждать с нетерпением","translation_kk":"асыға күту","definition":"To feel happy about something that will happen.","example":"I look forward to the holidays.","theme":"Emotions","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-22","word":"tear","translation":"die Träne","translation_ru":"слеза","translation_kk":"көз жасы","definition":"A drop of water that comes from your eye.","example":"A tear ran down her face.","theme":"Emotions","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-23","word":"unhappy","translation":"unglücklich","translation_ru":"несчастный","translation_kk":"көңілсіз","definition":"Not feeling happy.","example":"He felt unhappy when his friend left.","theme":"Emotions","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-24","word":"bored","translation":"gelangweilt","translation_ru":"скучающий","translation_kk":"іші пысқан","definition":"Feeling that nothing is interesting.","example":"I was bored on the long journey.","theme":"Emotions","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-25","word":"shocked","translation":"erschrocken","translation_ru":"потрясённый","translation_kk":"аң-таң болған","definition":"Very surprised or upset by something unexpected.","example":"She was shocked by the news.","theme":"Emotions","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-26","word":"be lucky","translation":"Glück haben","translation_ru":"повезти","translation_kk":"жолы болу","definition":"To have something good happen by chance.","example":"We were lucky to find the lost phone.","theme":"Emotions","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-27","word":"give a hug","translation":"umarmen","translation_ru":"обнять","translation_kk":"құшақтау","definition":"To put your arms around someone kindly.","example":"I gave my brother a hug.","theme":"Emotions","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-28","word":"roll","translation":"rollen","translation_ru":"катиться","translation_kk":"домалау","definition":"To move by turning over and over.","example":"The ball rolled down the hill.","theme":"Holidays","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-29","word":"against","translation":"gegen","translation_ru":"против","translation_kk":"қарсы","definition":"Opposing someone in a game or contest.","example":"We played against another team.","theme":"Holidays","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-30","word":"sure","translation":"sicher","translation_ru":"уверенный","translation_kk":"сенімді","definition":"Certain that something is true.","example":"I am sure this is the right path.","theme":"Communication","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-31","word":"careful","translation":"vorsichtig","translation_ru":"осторожный","translation_kk":"абай","definition":"Taking care to avoid a problem or danger.","example":"Be careful near the water.","theme":"Holidays","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-32","word":"free","translation":"kostenlos","translation_ru":"бесплатный","translation_kk":"тегін","definition":"Not costing any money.","example":"The museum was free.","theme":"Holidays","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-33","word":"pull","translation":"ziehen","translation_ru":"тянуть","translation_kk":"тарту","definition":"To move something towards you.","example":"Pull the door to open it.","theme":"Holidays","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-34","word":"bite","translation":"beißen","translation_ru":"кусать","translation_kk":"тістеу","definition":"To use your teeth to cut into something.","example":"Do not touch that animal; it may bite.","theme":"Holidays","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-35","word":"mean","translation":"bedeuten","translation_ru":"означать","translation_kk":"білдіру","definition":"To have a particular meaning.","example":"What does this word mean?","theme":"Communication","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-36","word":"just like","translation":"genau wie","translation_ru":"точно как","translation_kk":"дәл сондай","definition":"Very similar to someone or something.","example":"She sings just like her sister.","theme":"Communication","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-37","word":"outdoor","translation":"im Freien","translation_ru":"на открытом воздухе","translation_kk":"даладағы","definition":"Happening outside a building.","example":"We enjoy outdoor activities.","theme":"Holidays","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-38","word":"climb","translation":"klettern","translation_ru":"взбираться","translation_kk":"өрмелеу","definition":"To move up something using your hands or feet.","example":"We climbed the hill.","theme":"Holidays","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-39","word":"jacket","translation":"die Jacke","translation_ru":"куртка","translation_kk":"күртеше","definition":"A short coat for the upper body.","example":"Take a jacket for the evening.","theme":"Holidays","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-40","word":"pocket","translation":"die Tasche","translation_ru":"карман","translation_kk":"қалта","definition":"A small part of clothing for carrying things.","example":"My phone was in my pocket.","theme":"Holidays","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-41","word":"litter bin","translation":"der Abfalleimer","translation_ru":"мусорная урна","translation_kk":"қоқыс жәшігі","definition":"A container for rubbish.","example":"Put the paper in the litter bin.","theme":"Holidays","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-42","word":"apartment","translation":"die Wohnung","translation_ru":"квартира","translation_kk":"пәтер","definition":"A home that is part of a larger building.","example":"Dad lives in an apartment.","theme":"Holidays","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-43","word":"screen","translation":"der Bildschirm","translation_ru":"экран","translation_kk":"экран","definition":"The part of a device that shows pictures.","example":"We watched the film on a large screen.","theme":"Holidays","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-44","word":"fries","translation":"die Pommes frites","translation_ru":"картофель фри","translation_kk":"қуырылған картоп","definition":"Long thin pieces of potato cooked in oil.","example":"We ordered fries with our meal.","theme":"Holidays","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-45","word":"wash the dishes","translation":"Geschirr spülen","translation_ru":"мыть посуду","translation_kk":"ыдыс жуу","definition":"To clean plates and cups after a meal.","example":"I helped Dad wash the dishes.","theme":"Holidays","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-46","word":"century","translation":"das Jahrhundert","translation_ru":"век","translation_kk":"ғасыр","definition":"A period of one hundred years.","example":"The house is more than a century old.","theme":"Holidays","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-47","word":"land","translation":"landen","translation_ru":"приземляться","translation_kk":"қону","definition":"To arrive on the ground after flying.","example":"Our plane landed in the evening.","theme":"Holidays","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-48","word":"right now","translation":"jetzt gerade","translation_ru":"прямо сейчас","translation_kk":"дәл қазір","definition":"At this exact moment.","example":"I am busy right now.","theme":"Communication","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-49","word":"order","translation":"bestellen","translation_ru":"заказывать","translation_kk":"тапсырыс беру","definition":"To ask for food or a drink in a restaurant.","example":"We ordered pancakes.","theme":"Holidays","difficulty":"A2"},{"id":"access2-word-50","word":"road trip","translation":"die Autoreise","translation_ru":"автопутешествие","translation_kk":"көлікпен саяхат","definition":"A journey from place to place by car.","example":"We went on a road trip in summer.","theme":"Holidays","difficulty":"A2"}]
$access2$::jsonb) on conflict (id) do nothing;

insert into public.reading_passages (id, title, level, body)
select id, title, level, body from jsonb_populate_recordset(null::public.reading_passages, $access2$
[{"id":"access2-pony","title":"A surprise at the holiday cottage","level":"A2 · Access 2 p. 17 · Adapted retelling","body":"A family arrived at a holiday cottage on Dartmoor. It was a hot day, so they opened the doors and windows. They left cakes and flowers on the kitchen table and went outside.\n\nLater, they heard a noise in the cottage. A pony had walked inside and was eating the cakes. Amber took a photograph and shouted at it. The pony became frightened and knocked over the kitchen table.\n\nIt left marks on the carpet and knocked over a sofa before running outside. The family had expected a peaceful holiday, but their first day was a surprise."},{"id":"access2-abby","title":"Abby's news: a change of school","level":"A2 · Access 2 pp. 22–23 · Adapted retelling","body":"Abby and Maya were walking on the beach with Skip. The dog found a crab and would not leave it alone. Abby pulled him away, and Maya gave him a hug.\n\nMaya told Abby about visiting the Eden Project with Lucy and her grandparents. Maya liked the warm rainforest dome and its unusual plants. She did not enjoy walking around the gardens as much as Lucy did.\n\nThen Abby told Maya that she had to move to a boarding school. Her mum had been a pupil there. Abby was looking forward to climbing and sailing, but it was difficult to tell her friend. Maya was shocked and close to tears. Abby wanted them to keep texting, calling, and meeting in the holidays."},{"id":"access2-logbook","title":"Justin's USA trip: diary highlights","level":"A2 · Access 2 pp. 28–29 · Adapted retelling","body":"Justin stayed with his dad in Boston. They watched Dad's first film and ate hamburgers and fries. Justin helped wash the dishes. On a visit to Plymouth, Massachusetts, he bought a postcard for his mum.\n\nThey drove towards Baxter State Park. At Rosie's Diner, Justin ordered six pancakes but could not finish them. Dad ate the last two. Their campsite was beside a small river. During a swim in a nearby lake, Justin saw a moose and used Dad's phone to take a photo.\n\nThey climbed Mount Katahdin and enjoyed the view. One night, Justin woke up when he heard a strange sound. A black bear was near their food. Dad asked him to stay quiet, and eventually the bear left.\n\nBack in Boston, Dad helped Justin edit a film. At the end of the visit, Dad gave him his harmonica. Justin did not want his holiday to end."}]
$access2$::jsonb) on conflict (id) do nothing;

insert into public.reading_questions (id, prompt, options, answer, explanation, explanation_kk, passage_id)
select id, prompt, options, answer, explanation, explanation_kk, passage_id from jsonb_populate_recordset(null::public.reading_questions, $access2$
[{"id":"access2-rq1","prompt":"Why were the doors open?","options":["It was hot","The pony opened them","The family lost the key"],"answer":"It was hot","explanation":"The family opened the doors and windows because the day was hot.","explanation_kk":"Күн ыстық болғандықтан отбасы есіктер мен терезелерді ашты.","passage_id":"access2-pony"},{"id":"access2-rq2","prompt":"What frightened the pony?","options":["Amber's shout","The flowers","The cakes"],"answer":"Amber's shout","explanation":"Amber shouted, and the pony became frightened.","explanation_kk":"Amber айқайлағанда пони қорқып қалды.","passage_id":"access2-pony"},{"id":"access2-rq3","prompt":"Retell the main events in your own words. What caused the damage?","options":[],"answer":"The family left the doors open. A pony came inside to eat cakes. When Amber shouted, it became frightened and knocked things over before leaving.","explanation":"Include the open doors, the pony, the shout, and what happened next. Your tutor will review your wording.","explanation_kk":"Ашық есіктер, пони, айқай және одан кейін болған оқиғаны қос. Жауабыңды мұғалім тексереді.","passage_id":"access2-pony"},{"id":"access2-rq4","prompt":"What part of the visit did Maya enjoy?","options":["The rainforest dome","Walking through all the gardens","A swimming pool"],"answer":"The rainforest dome","explanation":"Maya liked the warmth and unusual plants in the rainforest dome.","explanation_kk":"Maya тропикалық орман күмбезінің жылуын және ерекше өсімдіктерін ұнатты.","passage_id":"access2-abby"},{"id":"access2-rq5","prompt":"What is Abby looking forward to?","options":["Outdoor activities","Never seeing Maya again","Changing her phone"],"answer":"Outdoor activities","explanation":"She mentions climbing and sailing at the new school.","explanation_kk":"Ол жаңа мектептегі өрмелеу мен желкенді қайықпен жүзуді айтады.","passage_id":"access2-abby"},{"id":"access2-rq6","prompt":"How does Maya feel about the news? Give one detail as evidence.","options":[],"answer":"Maya feels shocked and sad. She is close to tears when she learns Abby is leaving.","explanation":"Name a feeling and support it with a detail. More than one wording is possible.","explanation_kk":"Сезімді атап, оны мәтіндегі дерекпен дәлелде. Жауапты әртүрлі сөзбен жеткізуге болады.","passage_id":"access2-abby"},{"id":"access2-rq7","prompt":"Where did Justin order pancakes?","options":["At Rosie's Diner","At the campsite","At a school"],"answer":"At Rosie's Diner","explanation":"The diary describes breakfast at the diner.","explanation_kk":"Күнделікте дәмханада таңғы ас ішкені айтылған.","passage_id":"access2-logbook"},{"id":"access2-rq8","prompt":"What did Justin photograph near the lake?","options":["A moose","A black bear","A pony"],"answer":"A moose","explanation":"He used Dad's phone to photograph the moose.","explanation_kk":"Ол әкесінің телефонымен бұланды суретке түсірді.","passage_id":"access2-logbook"},{"id":"access2-rq9","prompt":"Which happened first?","options":["Breakfast at the diner","Climbing Mount Katahdin","Receiving the harmonica"],"answer":"Breakfast at the diner","explanation":"Breakfast came before camping and climbing; the gift came at the end.","explanation_kk":"Таңғы ас жорық пен өрмелеуден бұрын болды. Сыйлық сапар соңында берілді.","passage_id":"access2-logbook"},{"id":"access2-rq10","prompt":"Choose two diary events and explain why Justin might remember them.","options":[],"answer":"He might remember seeing a moose because it was unexpected, and the bear because it was frightening.","explanation":"Use events from the text and explain your reasons in your own words.","explanation_kk":"Мәтіндегі оқиғаларды таңдап, себебін өз сөзіңмен түсіндір.","passage_id":"access2-logbook"}]
$access2$::jsonb) on conflict (id) do nothing;

insert into public.writing_assignments (id, title, instructions, min_words, format)
select id, title, instructions, min_words, format from jsonb_populate_recordset(null::public.writing_assignments, $access2$
[{"id":"access2-u1-1","title":"Holidays and the weather","instructions":"Write 6–8 sentences about a real or imaginary holiday. Include where you were, who was with you, two weather words, two activities, and one negative sentence. Add a title and a short caption for a drawing. Use pages 10–13.","min_words":40,"format":"Book-based practice"},{"id":"access2-u1-2","title":"A new neighbour: past verbs","instructions":"Read page 14. Explain in two English sentences why Lucy is upset and what she does next. Then write six sentences about a visit last weekend using three regular and three irregular past verbs. Use pages 15–16 to check the forms.","min_words":40,"format":"Book-based practice"},{"id":"access2-u1-3","title":"Understanding words in context","instructions":"Read A pony came to tea on page 17. Choose five unfamiliar words, guess their meanings, and explain the clue for each. Then retell the story in 4–5 English sentences: arrival, the open house, the pony, the damage, and the ending. Use your own words.","min_words":40,"format":"Book-based practice"},{"id":"access2-u1-4","title":"Questions and phone conversations","instructions":"Write five questions about a friend's holiday: one yes/no question and four wh-questions. Answer them in English. Then write a six-line phone dialogue in which the person you want is not at home and you leave a message. Refer to pages 18–21. Audio tasks need the book's recordings.","min_words":40,"format":"Book-based practice"},{"id":"access2-u1-5","title":"Abby's news: negatives and feelings","instructions":"Read Abby's news on page 22 and use page 23 to check your understanding. Write one sentence about Abby's news, two about Maya's feelings with evidence, and four sentences about your own weekend: two positive and two negative. Use didn't with the base verb.","min_words":40,"format":"Book-based practice"},{"id":"access2-u1-6","title":"Notes and everyday English","instructions":"Using page 26, make a crib sheet for one holiday day: place, people, weather, three activities, and a feeling. Practise a one-minute talk with it. Submit your notes and a 4–6 sentence English retelling. Add a four-line lost-phone dialogue using page 27. Your tutor will assess speaking in the lesson.","min_words":40,"format":"Book-based practice"},{"id":"access2-u1-7","title":"My USA logbook","instructions":"Read My USA logbook on pages 28–29. List four activities Justin did and where he did them. Write two short diary entries about a real or imagined trip, using at least five past-tense verbs. Include one surprising event and how you felt. Review the irregular verbs on page 207.","min_words":40,"format":"Book-based practice"},{"id":"access2-u1-8","title":"A holiday brochure and reflection","instructions":"Using pages 30–31, write a 80–100 word brochure page about a place in Germany, Kazakhstan, or another country. Include the season, location, weather, three things visitors can do, and what you did or would like to do. Add a heading and caption. Finish by rating your vocabulary, notes, grammar, and layout: needs practice, OK, or confident.","min_words":80,"format":"Book-based practice"}]
$access2$::jsonb) on conflict (id) do nothing;
